Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
WG-5: the energy-momentum tensor from the variation of the tetrad\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ad4a0b70-70f9-40fd-990d-f0da505f936a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In general relativity the source of gravitation is the energy-momentum \
tensor, defined as the response of the action to a change of the metric. For \
a spinor the action depends on the tetrad, not only on the metric, and the \
response to the tetrad has a symmetric and an antisymmetric part. The check \
perturbs the flat tetrad by sixteen symbolic functions, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["a", "TI"]], 
     SuperscriptBox["", "\[Mu]"]}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Delta]", "+", 
     RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Mu]"}]]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128d11d4-4311-4a72-b167-c158523b60fe"],
 ", varies the Dirac action to first order in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "17c9066d-e000-41d7-b68c-2683185e60cf"],
 " with the package ",
 StyleBox["VariationalMethods",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", and shows: the symmetric part is exactly the tensor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "850a3992-a77a-479a-b9cf-fed7d8c0530c"],
 " of the manuscript (16.2), for any field; the antisymmetric part is not \
zero for an arbitrary field, but vanishes for a solution of the Dirac \
equation (a superposition of two plane waves of mass 3). So on solutions the \
tensor is symmetric, as Einstein's equations require."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4912c73b-2fc4-4c82-a1b9-e4494d8cb8d9"],

