complex frequency omega = a + i b (a, b, m, lambda real) the radial current \
obeys dJ/dr = 2 b (|P|^2 + |Q|^2) exactly for every r > 0; for a quasi-bound \
state, which decays at infinity, with J = 2 at the horizon (q_0 = 1), this \
gives Im omega = -1/N, N the integral of |P|^2 + |Q|^2 from the horizon to \
infinity [dJ/dr - 2 b (|P|^2 + |Q|^2) = 0]\"\>"], "Print",
