Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The numerical part: a series at the horizon and NDSolve", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2c051764-5640-4982-9248-bb997bebfdb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The next two checks find quasi-bound states and greybody factors again, \
independently of the Rust program. The solution that is smooth at the horizon \
is started from its Taylor series of order 20 at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "2", "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "20"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "113e5da9-8535-4ca4-93c5-b47d02c0f95c"],
 " (the coefficients come from a linear system that the cell builds once), \
and integrated with ",
 StyleBox["NDSolve",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " in arithmetic of 32 significant digits. This is an integration in the \
radius, not in time: ",
 StyleBox["NDSolve",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " uses its automatic method, which controls its error to the requested 26 \
digits."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ee31be05-3850-4428-a73e-dcc918996dca"],

