Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["WV-1: the separation for an arbitrary mass function", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7226a204-dd2e-4d47-9db9-bee4a7235ec8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the spin connection computed from the coframe for an arbitrary \
function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalM]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["LG",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["LG",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec15d009-9815-4a1c-9aa3-a9cbc7742be3"],
 ", the check shows that the separated spinor (24.1) solves the Dirac \
equation exactly when (18.4), (24.2) and (24.3) hold, for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14015ba1-4ab2-4b07-bb02-b7108015ae06"],
 ". As a control it changes one coefficient of (24.2) and shows that the \
identity then fails, so the check is able to fail."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c111b97b-d116-4e2b-8a70-2315de5c4509"],

