Cell[BoxData["\<\"PASS WV-4     (Rust LV-2; Python YV-4) the static solutions \
of stage 6 and the stationary solutions of stage 5 are the same field: if (P, \
Q) solve the system of stage 5 in the freely falling tetrad (W = \
(2/r)^(1/2)), then p = (1 + W)^(-1/2) e^(i omega h) P, q = (1 + W)^(1/2) e^(i \
omega h) Q with h' = 1/(1 + W) solve the static equations of stage 6 \
identically (written as rational functions of b = (1 + W)^(1/2)); with the \
opposite exponents, (1 + W)^(1/2) and (1 + W)^(-1/2), they do not (the \
control).  So the coframe of stage 6 is the freely falling coframe boosted \
with the rapidity -ln(1 + W), v = tau + h(r), and the two problems have the \
same quasi-bound frequencies [residuals {0, 0}; control (abbreviated) \
{(bb^8*pV - (2*I)*lam*qV - 4*mB*qV - 2*bb^6*(2*pV + I*lam*qV) + bb^4*(5*pV + \
(2*I)*lam*qV) - 2*bb^2*(pV - I*lam*qV + 2*mB*qV))/(bb*(-1 + bb^2)^3), \
((-2*I)*(-1 + bb^2)^2*(1 + bb^2)*lam*pV + 4*(1 + bb^2)*mB*pV + (-1 + \
bb^2)^2*qV)/(2*bb^3*(-1 + bb^2))}]\"\>"], "Print",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.004398277554286*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "During evaluation of \
In[340]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8a1626ae-85b9-4548-be5a-6968f1ad9a25"],

