Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. The pair bound by the zeugon (Part VI, Section 29)", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"fa03438d-13a4-4148-9925-04c5fa61be1d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two quasi-particles of the superfluid with opposite zeugon charges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45de0edd-01d6-4a2f-8c68-71f321e79ee1"],
 " attract each other through the massless zeugon, as an electron and a \
positron attract each other through the photon. Their bound states form an \
atom, the pair, with the potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
      StyleBox["LG",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["Z",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], "/", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0301eef3-fdc1-4bf9-9b50-6014f7c1c07b"],
 " and the strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["LG",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["Z",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["v",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "2"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"16", "\[Pi]"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fa4fc96-464a-44ae-b675-37a45b483867"],
 ". To leading order its levels are those of hydrogen with the reduced mass \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Mu]", 
    StyleBox["LG",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["pair",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f978238f-3801-4ed0-a3b0-bda099717d18"],
 "; at the next order, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
      StyleBox["LG",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["Z",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26430e48-7c10-4d4c-9584-f4097086e43b"],
 ", the motion of the particles (relativistic corrections), their spins (fine \
and hyperfine structure) and, for a particle with its own antiparticle, a \
term of virtual annihilation shift the levels. These corrections are computed \
from the Breit-Fermi Hamiltonian, as for positronium. In the code the units \
are those of the relative motion: reduced mass 1 and strength 1, so each \
particle has the mass ",
 StyleBox["m = 2",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "; ",
 StyleBox["rr",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " is the radius."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"108a29f0-55f7-4ebf-9a4e-9e0828a6ce06"],

