Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["WT-3: the energy in a weak static tidal field", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e45e3e6f-85ee-4cc0-a925-0e8a80032e5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In a weak static field the energy of the ground state shifts by \
second-order perturbation theory, which the method of Dalgarno and Lewis \
turns into a differential equation for one function. The check verifies that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Kappa]", 
     StyleBox["LG",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["tid",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], "3"], "/", "3", "+", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43885092-cb15-41ff-917f-3cc929f163a4"],
 " solves it, and that the energy is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["LG",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["tid",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox["1", "2"]}], "-", 
    FractionBox["15", "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[Kappa]", 
       StyleBox["LG",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["tid",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "2"], "-", 
    FractionBox["153", "2"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[Kappa]", 
       StyleBox["LG",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["tid",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "3"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2582bb18-62ae-4e22-98a3-364dbb5181a9"],
 " (32.5); the Python program compares these coefficients with the \
eigenvalues of its matrices."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c8512b4c-f64e-491e-ae4d-4d28cd1d07b4"],

