Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["WW-2: a set that is not a representation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2017339e-d573-4d1c-982c-000264568b6d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Lord writes that any linearly independent set of four Hermitian matrices \
will do; the manuscript shows that this is too much. The set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "0", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b7a728-a3cc-4624-8e42-af88fc3328d4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "1", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16c38835-d98d-4bb8-9bed-fd3a5b21d143"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "2", 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "100b7ac9-0627-47cc-ba09-d5567fabb8cf"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "3", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "0", 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "96a84b39-b694-4b4d-9abd-c15d28c0ff7a"],
 " is Hermitian and linearly independent, but the polarized determinant of \
the first and the last is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6301d2d-213f-4994-a2d8-6acaa036fb04"],
 " instead of 0, and their Dirac matrices do not anticommute. So a valid set \
must also satisfy (1.3)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c2bd441c-52d4-45da-8815-c07e7a0a73bb"],

