Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10. The remarks of the manuscript", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"0d36ab00-7ecf-44d7-91f1-259bc70b058a"],

Cell["\<\
The manuscript qualifies several of its results: it says where a result is an \
approximation, a model or restricted in some way, and its remarks document \
explains each such remark (what it means, why it holds, why it matters). Here \
they are in brief, with the chapter of this notebook that bears on each.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10d10e47-9547-489c-b6f5-e00e735c3299"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "R1, the coupling to the scalar curvature: the square of the Dirac operator \
contains ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox["1", "4"]}], 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a424085-4765-4593-9f92-3ba37bcd323a"],
 ", not Lord's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e699bba8-8115-4401-9169-f6afc8126cfe"],
 " (Chapter 2, WG-4)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"963baa57-8f1a-498a-99b2-f5a4992ba36c"],

Cell["\<\
R2, a constant Dirac mass and pair amplitude: Theorem L2 assumes that the \
Dirac mass and the pair amplitude of the quasi-particle are the same \
everywhere; the algebra that the theorem rests on is checked in Chapter 2 \
(WG-6).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d8862b58-7724-44fa-bd25-5cff7f3e8afd"],

Cell["\<\
R3, the energy of the condensed vacuum: the condensation lowers the energy of \
the vacuum, and gravitation responds to that as to a cosmological constant \
(computed by the Rust and the Python programs; not in this notebook).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4c59937f-2b80-4909-8fb6-5a7422ffc360"],

Cell["\<\
R4, operators, normal order and semiclassical gravitation: the interaction \
and the cutoff of the brochon are defined in flat space-time and have no \
unique form in a curved one; the source of Einstein's equations is the \
expectation value of the energy-momentum tensor of Chapter 2 (WG-5), which is \
called semiclassical gravitation.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6fc064eb-4521-4919-a9b8-c4ad36cc3e78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "R5, the massive gauge fields: in the superfluid ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "1"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63696b66-8574-440a-89c0-dddbe5aa6b24"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31261ab7-c4c1-4495-a071-db7b2e9de8f4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3eaf1911-f027-42af-9600-82b077faa526"],
 " are massive, and their energy-momentum tensors add to the source of \
gravitation; the manuscript needs only the tensor of the zeugon, which stays \
massless (Chapter 2, WG-6)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b35720e6-f496-4bcd-aae0-50d1dc5e39f3"],

Cell["\<\
R6, the small-mass formulas of the gravitational atom: the formulas of Dolan \
and Dempsey hold for small coupling only; the exact states are those of \
Chapter 3 (WS-7).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"254848a8-6bab-4dac-be0b-c8c417a51476"],

Cell["\<\
R7, the shrinking black hole is a model: a black hole that shrinks by \
evaporation is described by the ingoing Vaidya space-time with an inflow of \
negative energy (the model of W. A. Hiscock); the radiation that leaves is \
not modelled (Chapter 2, WG-3; Chapter 4).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c19398a0-cc25-4602-b7e2-e5d0d7d50f4e"],

Cell["\<\
R8, projections are not probabilities: the quasi-bound states of a black hole \
are not orthogonal, so the projections of the field on them do not add up to \
one (computed by the Rust program; not in this notebook).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e6377294-f812-493d-8ade-a5ab57191c43"],

Cell["\<\
R9, the polarization of the condensate is not computed: the potential of the \
pair is that of the empty vacuum; the superfluid could weaken it at long \
distances (Chapter 5 uses the unweakened potential).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b2413bd8-939f-4bf2-a788-c969f07e559f"],

Cell["\<\
R10, the estimate of the charge by the creation of pairs: Schwinger's rate of \
pair creation is used as an estimate of the largest charge (Chapter 6 checks \
the geometry and the accretion limit).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c872c6f3-5ee3-4a37-8c3b-9c37c8ce9b2f"],

Cell["\<\
R11, the ringing in the limit of large angular number: the relation between \
the shadow and the ringing holds for large angular number only (Chapter 6, \
WC-3).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"41e94931-b178-4d28-88d4-954ea5327be0"],

Cell["\<\
R12, the quadratic tidal potential and the slow relative motion: the tidal \
potential is the first term of an expansion in the size of the pair divided \
by the radius (Chapter 7, WT-2).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c942acf8-fa66-4df4-a1c6-6999a2240212"],

Cell["\<\
R13, the classical estimate of the break-up is false for a real fall: the \
barrier of Chapter 5 (WP-2) sinks much earlier than the pair actually \
separates.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2ffa8eae-da5c-487d-b8b3-3a147cc59ac1"],

Cell["\<\
R14, the probability of separation late in the fall depends on a numerical \
device: below the remaining time 1, the probability that the two \
quasi-particles are more than 10 Bohr radii apart depends on how the tidal \
potential is flattened far out (computed by the Rust program; not in this \
notebook).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"80d88deb-f9a6-4567-9208-ad4b17e83f76"],

Cell["\<\
R15, the uncertainties of the cosmological parameters enter the comparison of \
the vacuum energy with observation (not in this notebook).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"af1721aa-7074-41a7-b7f4-811babc2ce1d"],

Cell["\<\
R16, the conservation of the number of quasi-particles holds in the \
mean-field approximation (Chapter 8, WA-3).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"26ab58fb-8d36-4158-abea-41e115ff08fc"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

